<id/doc/doc_coriander/#concept> a <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E55_Type>, skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Coriander"@en ;
    skos:broader <id/grp/grp_spices_condiments/#concept> ;
    skos:definition "an umbelliferous plant, the *Coriandrum sativum*, grown for its pungent fruit, used as a seasoning in India, and for the essential oil expressed from the seeds, which are a warm and agreeable aromatic. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 119]"@en ;
    skos:inScheme <id/scheme/#resource> ;
    skos:notation "doc_coriander" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Coriander"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "Document-attested minor 19th-century commodity absent as a standalone line in Layer-1 British/Canadian customs ledgers; typically subsumed under htc:0408 (Spices Unenumerated). Attested in: P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 119, P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Products of the Vegetable Kingdom (1854, Project Gutenberg #15191)."@en ;
    <ontology/attestationBasis/#resource> "document_attested" ;
